  "irVersion": 8,
  "notes": {
    "ids": "The source of identifiers for new items.",
    "todos": "A to-do list. Items are added, completed, removed and listed. Each item has an identifier given by the list, a title, and whether it is done.",
    "todos.calcs.listed": "The items in the order they were added: all of them, only the open ones, or only the done ones, as asked.",
    "todos.does.add": "A title that is empty or made only of whitespace, or that has more than 100 characters (a title of exactly 100 is fine), is refused as invalid, with no item. Otherwise a new item with a fresh identifier and the given title, stored exactly as given (not trimmed), goes after the others, and the answer is created, with the item (not done).",
    "todos.does.complete": "An open item becomes done, and the answer is completed. An item that is already done stays done, and the answer is already-done. An unknown identifier is not found, and nothing changes.",
    "todos.does.remove": "The item is removed, and the answer is removed. An unknown identifier is not found, and nothing changes."
  },
